WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.410
A Sikh hymn describes countless
ages before the universe:

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.510
only darkness, stillness, and God alone.

3
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:13.920
Then, Sikhs believe, God made the
vast universe with a single word.

4
00:00:13.970 --> 00:00:16.960
Countless worlds, below and above.

5
00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.770
No one can count them.

6
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:22.080
The opening lines of Sikh
scripture, the Mool Mantra,

7
00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:25.930
call God Karta Purakh: the Creator Being.

8
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:29.340
But if God made everything,
where is God now?

9
00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:32.680
Inside the world, outside it, or both?

10
00:00:32.730 --> 00:00:37.330
In this mission, you'll read what the
Guru Granth Sahib says about the Creator.

11
00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:42.190
Then you'll see how this belief shapes
the way Sikhs treat nature and people.

12
00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:46.190
Your mission: find out where
Sikhs believe the Creator is,

13
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:47.490
and why it matters.
